{"name":"Palm Heart Cream","hex":"#ddd8c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"palm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various evergreen trees from the family Palmae or Arecaceae, which are mainly found in the tropics.","A branch or leaf of the palm, anciently borne or worn as a symbol of victory or rejoicing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inner and somewhat concave part of the human hand or other primate hand that extends from the wrist to the bases of the fingers.","The corresponding part of the forefoot of a nonprimate mammal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b7/Humhrt2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Human heart during an autopsy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHumhrt2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CG_Heart.gif/500px-CG_Heart.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Computer-generated animation of a beating human heart","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACG_Heart.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Heart_near.png/500px-Heart_near.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The human heart is in the middle of the thorax, with its apex pointing to the left.[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeart_near.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Heart_diseccion.jpg/500px-Heart_diseccion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Heart_diseccion.jpg/500px-Heart_diseccion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heart being dissected showing right and left ventricles, from above","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeart_diseccion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/2011_Heart_Valves.jpg/500px-2011_Heart_Valves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi